  "body": "Promotes the validated SCAN v0.24 development line into main while preserving frozen v0.23 unchanged.\n\nKey changes:\n- Adds adaptive substrate assimilation for unfamiliar or mechanically incomplete runtimes.\n- Adds deterministic TypeScript/React/Electron structural scanning and NEST/effect mapping learned from the Moji flexibility specimen.\n- Generates an inert assimilation workbench with evidence samples, candidate adapter/probe/test scaffolds, an LLM engineering brief, and promotion gates.\n- Adds `scan-body validate-assimilation` to test candidate adapters against a frozen specimen using a trusted baseline plus two fresh deterministic candidate scans.\n- Keeps candidate promotion blocked pending review; generated scanner code is never auto-promoted.\n- Filters incidental docs/test/vendor/deployment languages from runtime-substrate triggers.\n- Adds deterministic assimilation-workbench validation and clean source package-manifest self-audit.\n\nValidation on exact head `b68c989a1ce58fd0d8e78737ef2078d0a4938a3d`:\n- frozen v0.23 unchanged from main: PASS\n- v0.24 regression suite: PASS\n- frozen Moji identity: PASS\n- cold baseline: PASS\n- adaptive scan A/B: PASS\n- canonical output determinism: PASS\n- assimilation workbench determinism: PASS\n- mechanical comparison/integrity gates: PASS\n- package manifest regeneration/self-audit: PASS\n- final package manifest: 83/83 source files verified, zero audit issues\n\nMoji calibration at this checkpoint remains honest rather than claiming semantic completeness: 103 human surfaces, 96 bound, 38 closed surface\u2192effect/state routes, 58 partial, 7 unresolved, zero integrity errors. Remaining uncertainty continues to open a refinement workbench automatically.",
